From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:28:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] sharper default icons, drawn at icon size

Estuary's 117 single-colour Default*.png icons are 256 px, and the list
view's side panel stretched the icon of an item without artwork (the ..
entry, a folder) over its whole 540 x 470 poster area, ~1100 px on a 4K
screen: soft, jagged and oversized. The icons are re-rendered at 512 px from
their own shapes (alpha upscaled, the 50 % edge kept, a ~1 px anti-aliased
ramp at the new size; the ten multi-colour pictures are left as they were),
and an item with no poster or thumbnail of its own now shows its icon at
256 x 256, centred where a poster would stand: 512 px on a 4K screen, one to
one with the new icons. Posters, thumbnails and genre/studio art keep the
full panel.
